      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that you are just trying to refactor existing code. But this code is wrong.\n\n1)  Since in v3 username is unique within a domain, we can\u0027t get correct user id from user name\n2) Code assumes that  in case of external auth, client is going to send userid/password instead of username/pasword\n3)  So I can send any valid user id and not necessarily the remote_user\u0027s user id. This looks like  a security hole\n4)  Looks like password in request doesn\u0027t matter in case of external auth. Any password should work.\n\nAm is missing something here?",
